    "M-1785627567846": {
      "content": "Environment lesson (2026-08-01): systemd user units do NOT inherit an interactive shell's environment. GROQ_API_KEY was exported from ~/.bashrc, so an interactive 'model-manager.mjs check' showed 'groq: up' while the scheduler journal showed 'groq: not configured' on every tick. ALWAYS verify scheduler-affecting config from 'journalctl --user -u <unit>' after a real timer run, never from an interactive shell — an interactive run is what hid this. Scheduler-visible secrets belong in ~/.hermes/.env (mode 0600), which every sdlc-sched-* unit loads via EnvironmentFile=-%h/.hermes/.env.",
      "layer": "recent",
      "date": "2026-08-01",
